      "body": "Salvage follow-on for #7297 (queue task 14201), routed by triage task 13841.\n\nRe-applies the unique remainder of closed archive PR #7524 (`archive/janitor-2026-11-07/probe-dispatch-dechunk-wt`): the `probe_dechunked_len_huge_chunk_size` test in `pkgs/fleet/crates/fleet-dispatch/src/lib.rs`, absent from current main. Nothing else is changed.\n\n**Finding preserved.** The test pins the unchecked arithmetic in `dechunked_len` on the peer-declared chunk size: `ffffffffffffffff` (usize::MAX) and `fffffffffffffffe` (usize::MAX - 1) overflow `size + 2` and panic in debug/test builds. This is the exact evidence filed as #6512 (\"dechunked_len does unchecked arithmetic on the peer-declared chunk size\"), which remains open; the checked-arithmetic fix is Phase 3 of #6582 and is not part of this salvage.\n\n**Normalization.** The probe's diagnostic `println!`/`catch_unwind` report is expressed as assertions over the same two inputs so the test carries an oracle. The controls keep the existing pins (`Some(9)`, incomplete `None`) and show `dechunk()` handles the same bytes safely. The test deliberately pins the current overflow so the #6512 fix trips it and updates it.\n\n**Verification (laptop, this branch):**\n- `cd pkgs/fleet && cargo test -p fleet-dispatch probe_dechunked_len_huge_chunk_size` — 1 passed, 0 failed.\n- Diff vs main is exactly the salvaged test (29 insertions, 0 deletions) in the one in-scope file.\n\nClosed PR #7524 was not reopened and its archive branch was not recreated; it remains the preservation record and diff source.\n\nRefs #7297, #6512\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796794609&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7978&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7978&signature=7b1f472c53c127da2c0dcaa624f5ad76ca95d4e8191315488592f9e7c107b7e3\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-c