      "body": "## Summary\n\nBound repetition in the fleet-proxy response reader (issue #6509, Phase 2 of design #6582). The reader capped unit sizes (`MAX_LINE_BYTES`, `MAX_RESPONSE_BODY_BYTES`) but not repetition: the 1xx interim-head loop in `request()`, the header-line loop in `read_response_head()`, and the trailer-line loop in `read_chunked()` each consumed peer-controlled units forever, hanging the exchange and its pooled tunnel.\n\n- New named count bounds in `pkgs/fleet/crates/fleet-proxy/src/http.rs`: `MAX_INTERIM_HEADS` (16), `MAX_HEADER_LINES` (256), `MAX_TRAILER_LINES` (256) — sized generously above legitimate laptop-service behaviour.\n- Exceeding a bound returns `HttpError::Malformed` and marks the connection non-reusable, matching the existing size-cap failure shape.\n- Module doc now names the count bounds alongside the size bounds.\n- Tests: flood tests for all three loops (interim heads / header lines / trailer lines all fail Malformed + non-reusable) plus control cases (single interim head then final response; chunked body with trailers round-trips and stays reusable).\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `cargo test -p fleet-proxy` — all suites pass (lib 65/65; http module 24/24 including the 5 new tests).\n- `cargo fmt -p fleet-proxy -- --check` — passes.\n\n## Merge Danger\n\n**Door:** Two-way\n\n**Blast Radius:** Low — one file in fleet-proxy; bounds are far above any legitimate local-service response shape, and the failure shape (Malformed, non-reusable) is the one the reader already uses for size caps.\n\nFixes #6509\n\n🤖 Queue worker lane code-o, task 11388 (triage of record: task 11196).\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796690067&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=6998&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F6998&signature=f77e6b7a0b9e24de82b32c7dc82e543e0ac13441b75bef62165002f4d2c32f5a\"><pic