      "body": "Closes #8433.\n\n## Problem\n`read_response` in `pkgs/fleet/crates/fleet-dispatch/src/lib.rs` accepted invalid or truncated HTTP response framing: a malformed `Content-Length` was silently treated as absent (`value.parse().ok()`), duplicate lengths overwrote each other, `Transfer-Encoding` was accepted on a `contains(\"chunked\")` test, EOF ended the body loop for every framing shape (so a body cut short of its declared length — or cut inside a chunked stream — was returned as if complete; a partial body can be valid JSON, making the truncation silent), and `dechunk` tolerated chunks missing their CRLF terminator. This conflicts with #6582's present-but-invalid refusal contract.\n\n## Change\nStrict framing, validated where it is read:\n- **Headers:** every Content-Length statement (repeated headers, comma-joined values) must parse and all must agree — malformed or conflicting values are transport errors. Content-Length together with any Transfer-Encoding is refused as conflicting framing. Transfer-Encoding is accepted only as the single coding `chunked`; anything else (including `gzip, chunked`) is refused as unsupported.\n- **Body:** the reader now tracks an explicit `Framing` (length / chunked / close-delimited). EOF before a declared length is met, or anywhere inside a chunked stream (including its trailer section), is a truncation transport error naming the framing and the byte counts. Unframed bodies still run to connection close.\n- **Chunks:** one strict decoder (`parse_chunked`) distinguishes complete / incomplete / malformed: non-hex size lines and chunks missing their CRLF terminator are errors, never silent stops. The #6512 checked-arithmetic discipline is preserved (peer-declared sizes are checked before any slicing or allocation; the 64 MiB body bound still applies and the decoded body never exceeds the wire bytes). `dechunk`/`dechunked_len` are now wrappers over the strict parser.\n\n## Verification\n- `cargo test -p fleet-dispatch` — 16 passed, 0 failed, including 5 new tests: loopback (`TcpListener`) round-trips for length/chunked-with-trailer/agreeing-duplicate/unframed bodies; refusal of malformed, conflicting, and CL+TE framings and unsupported codings; refusal of truncation after valid JSON bytes and of mid-chunk/mid-size-line cuts; refusal of malformed chunk sizes and missing CRLF terminators; trailer-section completeness pins. The pre-existing #6512 huge-chunk-size pins still pass.\n- `cargo fmt -p fleet-dispatch` applied.\n\nQueue task 14827 (repo-health-code-pilot, lane code-h) — triaged inline and fixed in the same claim.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796955779&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=8434&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F8434&signature=bf826aa7909336c0dcf5ae7e91efb0a17d2f21cbe4d8375641bbf23645b39d92\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/8434?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
