      "body": "Queue task 6582, for issue #1395 (plan-of-record P2.3/P2.8: a planted bug in the voiding/frontier logic must fail the suites).\n\n## Change\n- `pkgs/id/tests/planted-bug-check.sh` (`just planted-bug-check`): requires the unmutated baseline to pass, then applies each named mutation from `tests/planted/` one at a time and requires its suites to FAIL, restoring files after every run.\n- `frontier-mapping.patch`: a group operation no longer contributes itself to the auth frontier (`CausalIndex::combine`). Caught (pre-existing from the earlier commits on this branch).\n- `voiding-authority.patch`: **moved in this PR's final commit.** Two earlier plants at `Engine::void` (`src/groups/delegation.rs`) survived `voiding_scenarios`/`voiding_properties` — those suites exercise authority voiding through the event store and have no delegation-grant coverage, so they never reach `Engine::void`. The plant now inverts the resolver-filter verdict in `Membership::is_effective` (`crates/id-core/src/membership/layer.rs`), the authority-voiding site the event-store resolve path actually runs: a removed member's concurrent operations take effect instead of being voided.\n\n## Verification (laptop, branch head a49d826f1)\n- `bash pkgs/id/tests/planted-bug-check.sh` exits 0: baseline green, voiding-authority caught, frontier-mapping caught.\n- Direct mutation run before wiring the patch: 7 `voiding_scenarios` S2 tests fail with the new plant (week-late add, transitive dependents, concurrent re-add, content-after-voided-add, voided-author stall).\n\n## Remaining gap (named, not hidden)\nDelegation-grant voiding scenarios reaching `Engine::void` still do not exist; the check documents this in the script and README instead of planting a mutation nothing can catch.\n\nRefs #1395.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796269543&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=4754&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F4754&signature=76e7d4d0d73e93b2cf5735dfe02bd92f6f81fc7436e1fa71bcde1a0bed325a67\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/4754?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
