      "body": "Fixes #6516\n\n## Problem\n`parse_request` in `pkgs/fleet/crates/fleet-proxy/src/serve.rs` collapsed every present-but-invalid `port` (70000, -1, 4801.5, \"4801\") to `None` via `.and_then(as_u64).and_then(u16::try_from().ok())`, and `Broker::do_request` turns `None` into the default `PORT_LAPTOP_AGENT` (4799) — a caller naming a bad port was silently rerouted to a service it never named.\n\n## Change\n- New `parse_port` at the frame boundary: absent (or null, mirroring `body`) stays `None` → the 4799 default downstream. A present-but-unusable port — string, float, bool/container, negative, zero, or > 65535 — returns an error naming the shape that arrived; `handle_request` wraps it in the standard `{status: 502, body: {error: \"broker: ...\"}}` frame and no connection is opened. Method/path already refuse malformed shapes at this boundary (#5750); the port now does too.\n- Port 0 rule (acceptance option): refused at the frame boundary, consistently with the other invalid values — not a dial attempt.\n- Doc comment on `parse_request` updated: port is the one strict field.\n\n## Tests (oracle: the shape rules in #6516 acceptance)\nNew unit tests in `serve.rs` pin the parse outcomes: absent/null port → `None` (routes to 4799), valid port (4801, 65535) → kept, and each invalid shape (70000, -1, 4801.5, \"4801\", 0, true) → refused with an error naming the port field. Verified by CI: `cargo test -p fleet-proxy`.\n\nQueue: task 11387 (repo-health-code-pilot), lane code-n.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796696430&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7053&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7053&signature=daa44dcc139eb4cebc78c62995fe7c275f2e19bfefc0e147ddc35ccb754add81\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7053?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Invalid or out-of-range port values now return a 502 response instead of silently using the downstream default. Missing or null ports continue to use the default.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
